260
00:16:52,225 --> 00:16:54,385
This is Wang Wuluan's unit.

261
00:16:55,145 --> 00:16:58,265
In the whole building,
this is the only apartment left for rent.

262
00:17:03,945 --> 00:17:06,825
-Are you alright?
-I'm fine.

263
00:17:28,105 --> 00:17:30,305
You actually paid rent for this?

264
00:17:30,385 --> 00:17:31,585
There are many units here.

265
00:17:31,665 --> 00:17:33,025
Couldn't you just pick one?

266
00:17:33,105 --> 00:17:35,145
You see, you're too green.

267
00:17:39,305 --> 00:17:41,945
Stop. Leave that for now.

268
00:17:42,705 --> 00:17:45,825
Put the kettle on, make tea,
and wait for visitors.

269
00:17:57,825 --> 00:17:59,265
This run-down place, jeez.

270
00:18:02,905 --> 00:18:03,945
Coming.

271
00:18:08,305 --> 00:18:09,465
Officer He.

272
00:18:10,305 --> 00:18:11,545
-Officer He.
-Come on in.

273
00:18:11,625 --> 00:18:12,785
Officer He.

274
00:18:13,705 --> 00:18:15,705
-Officer He, you moved in.
-It's messy.

275
00:18:15,785 --> 00:18:17,305
-Come in.
-Hello, Officer He.

276
00:18:17,385 --> 00:18:19,585
There's no need to hold back
in Officer He's place.

277
00:18:20,585 --> 00:18:25,065
Everyone, let's welcome Officer He
to his new home.

278
00:18:26,505 --> 00:18:27,745
Welcome!

279
00:18:27,825 --> 00:18:30,825
Officer He. Officer He.
You came at the right time.

280
00:18:30,905 --> 00:18:33,385
It's great. We have a capable man
on our side now.

281
00:18:33,465 --> 00:18:35,385
Exactly. A capable helper.

282
00:18:36,665 --> 00:18:38,785
I came here with a mission.

283
00:18:38,865 --> 00:18:42,385
I need you and everyone
to help me ask around.

284
00:18:42,465 --> 00:18:45,065
Everything about Officer Ran

285
00:18:45,145 --> 00:18:47,385
in Yuanlongli during the winter of 2002.

286
00:18:47,465 --> 00:18:50,265
Who he met. What he did. What he said.

287
00:18:50,345 --> 00:18:52,145
I want all of it.

288
00:18:52,785 --> 00:18:55,385
Don't worry. You can count on us.

289
00:18:55,465 --> 00:18:56,985
-Right.
-No problem.

290
00:18:57,065 --> 00:18:58,265
Of course.

291
00:18:58,345 --> 00:19:01,105
Looks like not everyone came today.

292
00:19:01,185 --> 00:19:03,185
I suggest we create a group chat.

293
00:19:03,265 --> 00:19:04,105
-Sure.
-Right.

294
00:19:04,185 --> 00:19:07,025
If anyone hears anything,
post it in the group.

295
00:19:07,105 --> 00:19:08,665
Right.

296
00:19:08,745 --> 00:19:10,545
Great idea!

297
00:19:10,625 --> 00:19:12,945
-Right.
-Good idea.

298
00:19:13,025 --> 00:19:15,665
Scan the code.

299
00:19:15,745 --> 00:19:16,705
HE YUANHANG

300
00:19:16,785 --> 00:19:18,105
DAD, DON'T LET THEM FOOL YOU
ONCE YOU'RE IN, IT'S HARD TO BACK OUT

301
00:19:27,505 --> 00:19:28,385
-Are you in?
-Yes.

302
00:19:28,465 --> 00:19:30,265
-All in?
-Yes.

303
00:19:31,705 --> 00:19:34,425
I only notified a few of you.
Who else is coming?

304
00:19:34,505 --> 00:19:35,905
-Isn't this everyone?
-Yeah.

305
00:19:35,985 --> 00:19:36,905
No one else.

306
00:19:44,985 --> 00:19:45,825
Officer He,

307
00:19:46,585 --> 00:19:49,545
this building is run-down and creepy.

308
00:19:49,625 --> 00:19:52,945
Moving in here is bad for your health.

309
00:19:53,825 --> 00:19:55,825
What if your situation relapses?

310
00:19:55,905 --> 00:19:57,545
You're not my son.

311
00:19:57,625 --> 00:19:59,425
-You don't need to worry about my health.
-He Yuanhang,

312
00:20:00,185 --> 00:20:02,665
you're not a police officer now,
and you're not an owner here either.

313
00:20:02,745 --> 00:20:05,705
Stop causing trouble
for the Redevelopment Bureau.

314
00:20:05,785 --> 00:20:06,625
Jeez.

315
00:20:07,465 --> 00:20:10,425
Open your eyes wide and look carefully.

316
00:20:10,505 --> 00:20:11,265
LEASE AGREEMENT

317
00:20:11,345 --> 00:20:14,745
There's a signature and a stamp.

318
00:20:15,425 --> 00:20:16,905
I'm a legal tenant.

319
00:20:16,985 --> 00:20:18,945
Who's causing trouble now?

320
00:20:20,105 --> 00:20:23,065
Money-grubber, you played tricks
on our demolition agreement.

321
00:20:23,145 --> 00:20:25,385
You promised compensation
and didn't deliver.

322
00:20:25,465 --> 00:20:28,905
If you want to tear down my home,
that'll be at least ten million.

323
00:20:29,505 --> 00:20:30,945
Not one single dime less.

324
00:20:31,025 --> 00:20:32,425
Ten million!

325
00:20:32,505 --> 00:20:33,945
Ten million!

326
00:20:34,025 --> 00:20:35,585
Ten million!

327
00:20:35,665 --> 00:20:37,465
Ten million!

328
00:20:37,545 --> 00:20:38,785
Ten million!

329
00:20:39,705 --> 00:20:41,145
-We did it!
-We won!

330
00:20:41,705 --> 00:20:43,105
Drink some tea.

331
00:20:43,185 --> 00:20:44,465
Drink tea.

332
00:20:44,545 --> 00:20:45,785
Carry on.

333
00:20:46,305 --> 00:20:47,385
Is the water ready?

334
00:20:47,465 --> 00:20:51,545
YUANLONGLI INTERNATIONAL GARDEN

335
00:20:53,905 --> 00:20:55,785
-Start the chant.
-Let's go.

336
00:20:55,865 --> 00:20:57,865
As long as we still have our homes,

337
00:20:57,945 --> 00:20:59,665
we can wait!

338
00:20:59,745 --> 00:21:01,505
Bad terms?

339
00:21:01,585 --> 00:21:03,625
We're not selling!

340
00:21:03,705 --> 00:21:05,585
As long as we still have our homes,

341
00:21:05,665 --> 00:21:07,185
we can wait!

342
00:21:09,585 --> 00:21:13,185
Dad, can't you clean up tomorrow?

343
00:21:14,185 --> 00:21:16,265
The real work hasn't even started.

344
00:21:16,345 --> 00:21:18,105
Go home and sleep
after everything is done.

345
00:21:19,705 --> 00:21:21,745
Are you sure you don't need me here?

346
00:21:21,825 --> 00:21:23,305
We're partners this time.

347
00:21:23,385 --> 00:21:25,105
I manage inside. You take the outside.

348
00:21:25,185 --> 00:21:26,945
We'll block them from both sides.

349
00:21:27,025 --> 00:21:28,905
There's no way we can't crack this case.

350
00:21:29,705 --> 00:21:31,225
Get up. Get to work.

351
00:21:36,745 --> 00:21:38,345
Open the windows wider.

352
00:21:47,985 --> 00:21:51,625
FAKE BLUE LEATHER HEELS

353
00:22:01,145 --> 00:22:05,025
Dad, even the task force
can't match this setup.

354
00:22:06,225 --> 00:22:09,105
Before troops move, supplies go first.

355
00:22:10,185 --> 00:22:13,465
Team Leader He, what are your next orders?

356
00:22:13,985 --> 00:22:15,705
I'm not a team leader.

357
00:22:16,225 --> 00:22:18,265
The team leader is Ran.

358
00:22:18,345 --> 00:22:19,665
What we need to do now

359
00:22:19,745 --> 00:22:22,185
is guess what his next move would be.

360
00:22:24,465 --> 00:22:26,025
If I were him,

361
00:22:27,105 --> 00:22:30,745
once I got to Yuanlongli,
I'd first use Tremaux's algorithm.

362
00:22:33,385 --> 00:22:35,145
I'll do the building canvass.

363
00:22:35,225 --> 00:22:38,505
Tomorrow, I'll go through every place
in this building

364
00:22:38,585 --> 00:22:39,985
connected to the June 30th case.

365
00:22:40,905 --> 00:22:41,945
I'll go to the property management

366
00:22:42,025 --> 00:22:44,865
and check the resident
and tenant list from 2002.

367
00:22:44,945 --> 00:22:47,145
And ask whether Uncle Ran
visited any of them back then.

368
00:22:47,745 --> 00:22:50,025
Good. That's the plan.

369
00:22:50,105 --> 00:22:52,305
Go home now. Rest up early.

370
00:23:01,345 --> 00:23:02,785
How come you're older now,

371
00:23:02,865 --> 00:23:04,145
but still full of energy?

372
00:23:04,745 --> 00:23:08,145
I have more than enough strength
to handle ten men alone.

373
00:23:10,065 --> 00:23:11,185
Remember to take
your blood pressure medicine.

374
00:23:11,265 --> 00:23:13,225
The wind gets strong at night.
Remember to close the windows.

375
00:23:13,305 --> 00:23:16,185
You're so naggy. Go on.

376
00:24:44,425 --> 00:24:47,105
I'm leaving, sir.

377
00:24:49,385 --> 00:24:50,225
Ran,

378
00:24:52,665 --> 00:24:54,625
you always saw me as your mentor.

379
00:24:57,505 --> 00:24:59,545
But you're the one who taught me.

380
00:25:28,385 --> 00:25:29,745
2002 YUANLONGLI RESIDENTIAL
COMPLEX OWNER/TENANT REGISTRATION FORM

381
00:26:48,545 --> 00:26:50,425
My goodness! Run!

382
00:26:50,505 --> 00:26:51,545
Hey!

383
00:27:38,545 --> 00:27:41,625
Du Mingliang, can I count you as a human?

384
00:27:41,705 --> 00:27:44,305
Playing games all day long.

385
00:27:44,385 --> 00:27:46,545
I'd rather have given birth
to a bun than you.

386
00:28:36,145 --> 00:28:37,505
Mr. He. Bollard!

387
00:28:41,865 --> 00:28:45,225
Mr. He, I heard you moved in.

388
00:28:46,865 --> 00:28:49,465
Many people moved out.
When are you planning to move?

389
00:28:49,545 --> 00:28:50,705
I'm not moving.

390
00:28:50,785 --> 00:28:52,705
I signed a long-term lease.

391
00:28:53,305 --> 00:28:54,545
I spent a lot of money
renovating the shop.

392
00:28:55,145 --> 00:28:56,625
That money-grubber

393
00:28:56,705 --> 00:28:58,745
tries to tear down illegally
and not pay me a dime.

394
00:28:58,825 --> 00:29:01,425
That's ridiculous.
I'm fighting him to the end.

395
00:29:02,865 --> 00:29:03,865
Join this group chat.

396
00:29:05,465 --> 00:29:07,625
Holdouts Group? What's this for?

397
00:29:07,705 --> 00:29:08,585
We're all on the same side.

398
00:29:08,665 --> 00:29:10,345
Oh, so you made a group there.

399
00:29:11,825 --> 00:29:14,105
Mr. He, why did you move in
at a time like this?

400
00:29:14,185 --> 00:29:15,265
Working on a case?

401
00:29:15,905 --> 00:29:17,145
Let me ask you this.

402
00:29:17,225 --> 00:29:19,385
In the winter of 2002,

403
00:29:19,465 --> 00:29:21,025
did you see Officer Ran?

404
00:29:25,545 --> 00:29:27,665
I wasn't supposed to tell you.

405
00:29:28,385 --> 00:29:30,825
But now I guess I can.

406
00:29:31,985 --> 00:29:32,825
Go on.

407
00:29:34,305 --> 00:29:35,865
Come out here!

408
00:29:35,945 --> 00:29:38,185
If you don't give me back the mouse,

409
00:29:38,265 --> 00:29:39,665
I'll go on a hunger strike for a month!

410
00:29:39,745 --> 00:29:41,145
Oh, I'm so scared of you.

411
00:29:41,225 --> 00:29:42,865
A whole month of hunger strike?

412
00:29:44,465 --> 00:29:46,385
-Madam.
-Officer Ran,

413
00:29:46,465 --> 00:29:48,065
perfect timing.

414
00:29:48,145 --> 00:29:50,905
Help me drag this brat out.

415
00:29:50,985 --> 00:29:53,825
You won't let me be a cybercafe manager
or open a cybercafé.

416
00:29:53,905 --> 00:29:55,945
Then I'll open the window
and live on air then.

417
00:29:56,025 --> 00:29:57,265
Go ahead.

418
00:29:57,345 --> 00:29:58,865
No one's scared of you.

419
00:30:03,345 --> 00:30:05,305
Du Mingliang, listen to me.

420
00:30:05,385 --> 00:30:07,865
Whether to be a manager
or open a cybercafé,

421
00:30:07,945 --> 00:30:09,465
you first need technical skills.

422
00:30:09,545 --> 00:30:11,425
There are courses online now.

423
00:30:11,505 --> 00:30:14,305
You can sign up for computer science
and study at home.

424
00:30:15,345 --> 00:30:16,305
Where did you see that?

425
00:30:16,905 --> 00:30:19,265
I can register it for you.
But first, you need to eat.

426
00:30:21,065 --> 00:30:23,185
Come out first.

427
00:30:23,265 --> 00:30:24,705
Eat your dinner.

428
00:30:30,225 --> 00:30:31,625
Jeez.

429
00:30:32,745 --> 00:30:35,545
Madam, let me ask you something.

430
00:30:35,625 --> 00:30:39,265
Did you see any strangers
go into No. 1703 this summer?

431
00:30:39,345 --> 00:30:41,345
You mean the Wu family?

432
00:30:42,065 --> 00:30:44,985
Their door is always shut.

433
00:30:45,065 --> 00:30:46,905
I only saw it open once.

434
00:30:46,985 --> 00:30:49,385
At the time,
the whole place was full of police.

435
00:30:58,665 --> 00:31:02,665
Right, have you seen
double-layer leather shoes?

436
00:31:03,305 --> 00:31:04,345
What is that?

437
00:31:04,985 --> 00:31:07,665
Shoes with one layer inside
and another layer wrapped outside.

438
00:31:07,745 --> 00:31:09,145
Counterfeit designer shoes.

439
00:31:11,225 --> 00:31:12,825
I have seen

440
00:31:12,905 --> 00:31:14,545
cardboard shoes before.

441
00:31:14,625 --> 00:31:16,585
Whoever made those
double-layer leather shoes

442
00:31:17,505 --> 00:31:19,985
must've had something wrong up top.

443
00:31:20,065 --> 00:31:21,545
Why wrap another layer

444
00:31:21,625 --> 00:31:23,625
over a perfectly good pair of shoes?

445
00:31:24,465 --> 00:31:26,065
I have seen that kind of shoes.

446
00:31:26,145 --> 00:31:27,745
The person making shoes like that

447
00:31:27,825 --> 00:31:29,985
must be a very experienced craftsman.

448
00:31:30,785 --> 00:31:32,825
Think about it. Two layers of leather

449
00:31:32,905 --> 00:31:35,865
and still made to look
exactly like the real thing.

450
00:31:35,945 --> 00:31:38,465
You know, that's not easy.

451
00:31:38,545 --> 00:31:39,985
Do you know any craftsmen like this?

452
00:31:41,185 --> 00:31:42,225
No.

453
00:31:43,185 --> 00:31:46,425
But you can ask those who sell fake shoes.

454
00:31:46,505 --> 00:31:48,545
They would definitely know.

455
00:31:51,865 --> 00:31:53,705
<i>Then Officer Ran left.</i>

456
00:31:54,665 --> 00:31:56,945
Before leaving,
he specifically told me this.

457
00:31:57,025 --> 00:31:58,385
If I ran into you,

458
00:31:58,465 --> 00:32:01,025
I must not tell you that he had come by

459
00:32:01,105 --> 00:32:03,425
or what questions he asked.

460
00:32:04,145 --> 00:32:06,545
Mr. He, aren't you his mentor?

461
00:32:06,625 --> 00:32:07,825
Why would he hide it from you?

462
00:32:09,225 --> 00:32:10,425
Double-layer leather shoes.

463
00:32:12,185 --> 00:32:13,625
Fake shoe sellers.

464
00:32:16,185 --> 00:32:18,945
Right. Guess what I saw
at the night market.

465
00:32:19,465 --> 00:32:21,865
Those same blue leather heels
the missing woman wore

466
00:32:21,945 --> 00:32:23,185
are called Double Fish.

467
00:32:23,265 --> 00:32:25,225
Seems like a name brand. Pretty expensive.

468
00:32:26,865 --> 00:32:30,025
So why didn't you clear your head too?

469
00:32:30,745 --> 00:32:33,385
You think branded shoes sold
at the night market are real?

470
00:32:37,985 --> 00:32:40,545
Mr. He. You're leaving?

471
00:32:40,625 --> 00:32:42,705
Put the property list aside for now.

472
00:32:42,785 --> 00:32:44,145
Go to the Commerce Bureau.

473
00:32:44,225 --> 00:32:45,985
Check the list of shoe and hat vendors

474
00:32:46,065 --> 00:32:48,785
at the Riverside Night Market in 1997.

475
00:32:49,345 --> 00:32:50,785
Contact them one by one.

476
00:32:50,865 --> 00:32:53,345
Ask whether Ran went
looking for them back then.

477
00:32:53,425 --> 00:32:54,865
<i>All vendors?</i>

478
00:32:54,945 --> 00:32:56,105
Every single one.

479
00:32:56,185 --> 00:32:57,865
<i>That's a huge workload.</i>

480
00:32:57,945 --> 00:32:58,945
Hurry up.

481
00:32:59,745 --> 00:33:01,425
Give us a straight answer.

482
00:33:01,505 --> 00:33:04,025
Can the relocation payout
still be negotiated or not?

483
00:33:04,105 --> 00:33:07,105
Otherwise, we old folks here
would rather die

484
00:33:07,185 --> 00:33:09,505
right here in Yuanlongli.

485
00:33:09,585 --> 00:33:11,745
Right! We'll die right here in Yuanlongli!

486
00:33:11,825 --> 00:33:13,185
As long as we still have our homes,

487
00:33:13,265 --> 00:33:15,225
we can wait!

488
00:33:15,305 --> 00:33:16,945
Bad terms?

489
00:33:17,025 --> 00:33:18,385
We're not selling!

490
00:33:18,465 --> 00:33:20,385
Everyone, please calm down.

491
00:33:20,465 --> 00:33:22,345
Kick up all the fuss you want.

492
00:33:22,425 --> 00:33:24,665
Not one extra dime
will be added to the compensation.

493
00:33:24,745 --> 00:33:26,305
-You!
-When the time comes,

494
00:33:26,385 --> 00:33:28,425
I'll bring the demolition crew
and bury explosives here.

495
00:33:28,505 --> 00:33:29,425
Whoever won't leave,

496
00:33:29,505 --> 00:33:31,425
I'll bury explosives at their front door.

497
00:33:31,505 --> 00:33:33,905
-How can you say this?
-Qian, you bastard!

498
00:33:33,985 --> 00:33:34,985
If you dare do that,

499
00:33:35,065 --> 00:33:36,665
I'll drag you down with me!

500
00:33:36,745 --> 00:33:38,745
Exactly! Go down together!

501
00:33:39,465 --> 00:33:41,065
-Alright, everyone.
-Go down together!

502
00:33:41,145 --> 00:33:42,945
Will you stop already?

503
00:33:43,025 --> 00:33:45,785
I'm the project manager here.
You just need to cooperate.

504
00:33:45,865 --> 00:33:46,705
We're all old neighbors.

505
00:33:46,785 --> 00:33:48,425
Is there any point in bluffing
and tricking them like this?

506
00:33:49,265 --> 00:33:50,105
I cooperate with you?

507
00:33:51,025 --> 00:33:53,985
Everyone from Yuanlongli knows
what kind of person you used to be.

508
00:33:59,465 --> 00:34:02,505
Some people have dirty minds.

509
00:34:02,585 --> 00:34:03,745
So everything they see looks dirty.

510
00:34:06,105 --> 00:34:06,945
Officer He,

511
00:34:07,665 --> 00:34:09,824
this is a matter for the owners.

512
00:34:09,905 --> 00:34:11,784
You're just a tenant.
You don't get a share of the money, right?

513
00:34:14,145 --> 00:34:16,985
Qian, you're not young anymore.

514
00:34:17,784 --> 00:34:19,665
You should really do something
about your bad breath.

515
00:34:21,025 --> 00:34:22,385
Well said!

516
00:34:22,465 --> 00:34:24,344
Exactly right!

517
00:34:26,865 --> 00:34:27,985
Let me make this clear.

518
00:34:28,065 --> 00:34:31,665
Everyone should raise demands
reasonably and legally.

519
00:34:31,744 --> 00:34:33,304
Don't act without order.

520
00:34:33,985 --> 00:34:36,264
Qiao is only doing her job.

521
00:34:36,344 --> 00:34:37,865
But the way she handles things

522
00:34:37,945 --> 00:34:39,784
is nothing like certain people.

523
00:34:40,385 --> 00:34:42,824
So don't lash out at everybody.

524
00:34:42,905 --> 00:34:44,145
Can you do that?

525
00:34:49,505 --> 00:34:52,505
Can't do it? Then I'm leaving
the group chat right now.

526
00:34:53,105 --> 00:34:54,705
-Please!
-No!

527
00:34:54,784 --> 00:34:56,625
-Officer He!
-Officer He,

528
00:34:57,385 --> 00:34:59,785
what you just said
was deeply philosophical.

529
00:35:00,505 --> 00:35:03,505
From now on, we won't
make things hard for Miss Qiao.

530
00:35:03,585 --> 00:35:04,425
-We won't do that.
-That's right.

531
00:35:04,505 --> 00:35:05,305
We won't do that to her.

532
00:35:05,385 --> 00:35:06,505
No.

533
00:35:07,505 --> 00:35:09,985
We'll go after the one
who's really to blame.

534
00:35:10,065 --> 00:35:11,385
-That's right.
-We'll go after the one

535
00:35:11,465 --> 00:35:12,425
who's really to blame.

536
00:35:12,505 --> 00:35:14,545
As long as we still have our homes,

537
00:35:14,625 --> 00:35:16,385
we can wait!

538
00:35:16,465 --> 00:35:18,305
Bad terms?

539
00:35:18,385 --> 00:35:20,585
As long as we still have our homes…

540
00:35:20,665 --> 00:35:22,785
As long as we still have our homes,

541
00:35:22,865 --> 00:35:24,825
we can wait!

542
00:35:24,905 --> 00:35:26,705
Bad terms?

543
00:35:26,785 --> 00:35:28,785
We're not selling!

544
00:35:28,865 --> 00:35:30,985
Qiao, don't worry.

545
00:35:31,065 --> 00:35:33,425
As long as I'm here,
nothing will go wrong.

546
00:35:34,185 --> 00:35:35,745
Thank you, Mr. He.

547
00:35:36,665 --> 00:35:40,025
There's something I'd like
to ask for your help with.

548
00:35:41,945 --> 00:35:42,785
Can you think of a way

549
00:35:42,865 --> 00:35:45,785
to delay the demolition deadline
a little longer?

550
00:35:46,465 --> 00:35:47,505
Mr. He,

551
00:35:48,345 --> 00:35:51,105
why did you get involved in this too?

552
00:35:51,185 --> 00:35:53,185
Ran left with regret.

553
00:35:54,665 --> 00:35:57,505
I have to stay in Yuanlongli for a while

554
00:35:57,585 --> 00:36:00,225
and help him make up for it
and fulfill his wish.

555
00:36:08,465 --> 00:36:09,305
Alright.

556
00:36:10,225 --> 00:36:11,465
I'll do my best to help.

557
00:36:26,585 --> 00:36:28,545
Mister, please do me a favor.

558
00:36:28,625 --> 00:36:30,145
I'll remember you for life.

559
00:36:41,665 --> 00:36:43,705
TO LET

560
00:36:53,345 --> 00:36:54,305
CALL

561
00:36:57,625 --> 00:36:58,625
<i>Hello?</i>

562
00:36:58,705 --> 00:36:59,985
Hello?

563
00:37:00,065 --> 00:37:02,385
I'd like to ask about the shop
you had for rent.

564
00:37:02,465 --> 00:37:05,145
Did you rent it to a woman
who sold shoes in 1997?

565
00:37:05,785 --> 00:37:07,945
<i>1997? I can't remember.</i>

566
00:37:08,025 --> 00:37:09,985
She had short hair and was very outgoing.

567
00:37:10,065 --> 00:37:11,745
Whenever someone passed her shop,

568
00:37:11,825 --> 00:37:13,625
she'd pull them over to look at her shoes.

569
00:37:14,225 --> 00:37:15,665
And she would say things like,

570
00:37:16,465 --> 00:37:18,305
"Please do me a favor, mister.

571
00:37:18,385 --> 00:37:20,865
I'll remember you for life."

572
00:37:21,505 --> 00:37:23,985
<i>Now I remember. That must be Liu Guifang.</i>

573
00:37:24,065 --> 00:37:25,705
<i>She couldn't afford the rent anymore.</i>

574
00:37:25,785 --> 00:37:27,225
<i>She insisted on using</i>
<i>her stock to cover it.</i>

575
00:37:27,305 --> 00:37:28,625
<i>Those were the exact words she used.</i>

576
00:37:29,225 --> 00:37:31,265
<i>I felt soft-hearted at the time,</i>
<i>so I let it slide.</i>

577
00:37:31,345 --> 00:37:32,545
Where did she go after that?

578
00:37:52,665 --> 00:37:55,105
I called you.
Why was your phone off again?

579
00:37:55,185 --> 00:37:57,585
Do you know how many vendors

580
00:37:57,665 --> 00:37:58,985
there were at
Riverside Night Market in 1997?

581
00:37:59,585 --> 00:38:00,505
More than 500.

582
00:38:00,585 --> 00:38:02,305
Even if I had three phones,
they would all be dead by now.

583
00:38:03,865 --> 00:38:04,865
Did you find anything?

584
00:38:06,705 --> 00:38:11,225
Uncle Ran contacted
someone named Liu Guifang.

585
00:38:12,225 --> 00:38:13,185
Here.

586
00:38:13,265 --> 00:38:14,105
LIU GUIFANG

587
00:38:44,025 --> 00:38:45,945
MAHJONG AND TEA,WELCOME INSIDE

588
00:38:48,345 --> 00:38:51,065
<i>I heard Liu Guifang got together</i>
<i>with the owner of a mahjong parlor.</i>

589
00:38:51,145 --> 00:38:52,505
<i>He received a hefty demolition payout</i>

590
00:38:52,585 --> 00:38:54,105
<i>from several houses</i>
<i>he owned in the village.</i>

591
00:38:54,185 --> 00:38:55,225
<i>He got rich long ago.</i>

592
00:39:12,345 --> 00:39:14,745
Come on. Be generous.

593
00:39:14,825 --> 00:39:16,705
Just do me a favor, mister.

594
00:39:16,785 --> 00:39:18,265
I'll remember you for life.

595
00:39:22,585 --> 00:39:24,985
Alright. I'm hanging up now, Yao.

596
00:39:26,425 --> 00:39:28,625
-Excuse me.
-Playing mahjong?

597
00:39:28,705 --> 00:39:30,305
Five years ago,
at the Riverside Night Market,

598
00:39:30,385 --> 00:39:32,105
you sold me a pair of fake leather shoes.

599
00:39:32,185 --> 00:39:33,185
They were cardboard shoes.

600
00:39:33,265 --> 00:39:34,945
What? Five years ago?

601
00:39:39,185 --> 00:39:40,185
It's been five years.

602
00:39:40,785 --> 00:39:43,905
Mister, you really hold grudges.

603
00:39:45,745 --> 00:39:47,545
I definitely don't remember you.

604
00:39:47,625 --> 00:39:49,545
But back then, I did sell fake shoes.

605
00:39:50,625 --> 00:39:53,305
How about this?
I'll pay you ten times the price.

606
00:39:53,385 --> 00:39:54,625
Is that okay?

607
00:40:02,865 --> 00:40:04,985
You sold Double Fish back then.

608
00:40:05,065 --> 00:40:06,065
They came in several colors.

609
00:40:06,145 --> 00:40:07,185
Do you know who in Weiyang

610
00:40:07,265 --> 00:40:09,105
could make this kind
of double-layer leather heels?

611
00:40:09,185 --> 00:40:10,665
Double-layer leather heels?

612
00:40:11,265 --> 00:40:12,585
Let me see.

613
00:40:14,625 --> 00:40:15,625
Don't open it.

614
00:40:18,465 --> 00:40:20,625
Double-layer leather heels…
That's pretty unusual.

615
00:40:21,225 --> 00:40:23,545
Judging from the finish and workmanship,

616
00:40:23,625 --> 00:40:26,225
that should be Mr. Lu
from Pingzhao County.

617
00:40:27,065 --> 00:40:28,105
Bet you didn't know.

618
00:40:28,185 --> 00:40:30,825
Mr. Lu was a master
of fake shoes in Weiyang.

619
00:40:30,905 --> 00:40:32,985
The shoes he made
could pass for the real thing.

620
00:40:34,225 --> 00:40:35,625
Pingzhao County.

621
00:40:38,785 --> 00:40:39,945
MAP

622
00:40:41,985 --> 00:40:45,145
PINGZHAO COUNTY

623
00:40:57,225 --> 00:41:00,505
PINGZHAO COUNTY

624
00:41:01,265 --> 00:41:02,505
It's been 13 years.

625
00:41:03,305 --> 00:41:05,945
No idea whether Mr. Lu is still around.

626
00:41:08,105 --> 00:41:09,665
NO. 6, LU VILLAGE, BEISHI TOWN
PINGZHAO COUNTY, WEIYANG CITY

627
00:41:09,745 --> 00:41:12,465
Uncle Ran probably
has taken this road too.

628
00:41:15,665 --> 00:41:17,465
We've picked the trail back up at last.

